;
; facemill-plate.ngc - face one side of a fixture plate blank.
;
; Copyright (C) 2026 narrativecollapse.  Free software under the WTFPL,
; version 2, with no warranty: see LICENSE.
;
; The blank is a 6.000 x 2.500 x 0.500 aluminium plate for one of the
; fixture plates in chapter 14 of "Machining the AR15 Lower Receiver
; Forging" by Ray Brandes.
;
; Datums: X0 Y0 at the blank's top left corner, so it runs to X6.000
; Y-2.500.  Z0 on its top surface; this takes 0.005 off.
;
; The face mill starts and finishes off the plate, and makes passes
; along its length.
;


; -- settings ---------------------------------------------------------

#<clear_z> = 0.500

#<tool> = 2             ; face mill: set the number and diameter to yours
#<tool_dia> = 1.500
#<rpm> = 2000
#<feed> = 15

#<length> = 6.000
#<width> = 2.500
#<cut_z> = -0.005


; -- program ----------------------------------------------------------

o<ar15-start> call [#<clear_z>]
o<ar15-tool> call [#<tool>] [#<rpm>] [#<feed>] [#<tool_dia>]

; The "walls" sit outside the plate so the cutter's centre runs from
; 0.100 off one end to 0.100 off the other, and covers the plate's edges
; along the sides.
o<ar15-pocket> call [-#<tool_dia> - 0.100] [#<tool_dia> / 2] [#<length> + #<tool_dia> + 0.100] [-#<width> - #<tool_dia> / 2] [0] [#<cut_z>] [#<tool_dia>] [#<tool_dia> / 2] [0.050] [0]

o<ar15-end> call
m2
